From 4f8a9325228d2b1dae6ebd9f31b4effb573259cd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 13:35:02 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Add the depth layouts and a 3D Video Settings window

Qt Multimedia's VideoOutput now draws the two views of a video that comes
with its depth map (2D plus depth: packed in the frame, an H.265 depth
layer, or a depth stream of its own) with libstereo-dibr, and shows them as
full side by side 3D video, with every choice of how they are drawn as a
property. Dragon Player gets them:

- The Input Format list of the 3D Video menu names the depth layouts:
  picture and depth map side by side, either first; one above the other,
  either first; with graphics (HDMI 1.4a's "L + depth + graphics +
  graphics-depth"); over a background.
- The menu turns the views from depth maps on and off, and opens a 3D Video
  Settings window and KDE's display settings (kcmshell6 kcm_kscreen), where
  the screen's 3D mode is chosen.
- The 3D Video Settings window, in a window of its own so that the video
  stays in sight: Enable 3D, Display Settings, the shape fallback, the
  resizing filter of half size views and the color depth of the 3D views;
  and for videos with a depth map, the picture as the left eye or the
  middle, the warping, the fill of uncovered areas and its neighbourhood,
  the smoothing of the depth, the range, the screen position, the shift,
  what a depth sample means with its near and far distances, and a whole
  Stereo3DDepth mark.

The choices are kept (QtCore's Settings, group 3DVideo) and the video
output is bound to them, the view chosen in the menu too; every change
applies at once, to a paused frame as well.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 via Claude Code
(cherry picked from commit a37326e2a1b4b96dee4fe0e54eec1af9366ef4aa)
